      "message": "fix(setup): moving operations into a setup keeps the program order\n\nSetOperationSetup cleared the moved operation's position. The program\norder puts an operation without a position last, in name order, so ops\nmoved one by one into a new setup came out in name order (a tap before\nits tap drill).\n\nThe moved operation now lands last in its target setup, through the\nsame append_position helper as CreateOperation. Undo restores the\npinned siblings. A move that keeps the effective setup (implicit None\nto the first setup) keeps its position.\n\nPinned by setup_move_order (command) and\nmcp_setup_moves::moving_operations_into_a_named_setup_keeps_the_program_order.\n\nFixes #3022\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
